course: dictionary
lesson: 12361
title: Informal words and their meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are informal. People use them in chat, stories and cartoons, but you will not often see them in a school essay. Critter is one of these words. Context helps you understand it. «Some critter's been in the bins» means an animal has been in the bins, because animals often dig through bins for food.
explain: Critter is a friendly, shortened form of creature. In the US and Canada, people talk about woodland critters like raccoons and skunks. When a critter is a small animal, you can swap in the word animal and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: A critter can also be a person, but only in a joking or fond way. If someone calls a child «You little critter!» with a smile, they mean the child is cheeky but lovable. Check the feeling in the sentence, not just the word itself.
fact: «Critter» means any creature or animal, especially a small one.
fact: «Critter» is informal, so you hear it in chat, cartoons and westerns more than in school writing.
fact: In the US and Canada, people talk about woodland critters such as raccoons and skunks.
fact: «Critter» can also mean a person, said in a joking or fond way.
fact: «Critter» comes from the word «creature».
exercise: «A critter ran across the path and into the long grass.» What is the critter in this sentence? | A road | A kind of rain | *An animal | A tree
exercise: Dad points and says, «Look at that little critter by the bins!» What does critter mean? | A cloud | A dustbin | A loud bird | *A small animal, like a cat or a fox
exercise: Gran laughs and says to her cheeky grandson, «You little critter!» What does critter mean here? | *A joking, fond name for a person | A bird that sings at night | A toy robot | A rude word for a bedroom
test: «Some critter's been in the bins.» What does critter mean in this sentence? | A child who is lost | *An animal | A nasty smell | A tin
test: Which animals are called woodland critters in North America? | Penguins and polar bears | Camels and lions | Dolphins and whales | *Raccoons and skunks
exam: Critter comes from which word? | critical | crater | *creature | cracker
